## Impact 

In the access-control scheme of the protocol, the devs have implied that there will be a single multisig that will be applied to all roles defined in the system. By having essentially an escape-hatch to that model, access control to all protocol funds can be bypassed by a form of "shadow administrator" with control over any token the protocol controls, simply by approving the maximum amount of funds to an arbitrary address.  

Operators can use this function to rug the protocol at whatever pace they desire.  All it requires is a single transaction to approve spending the full amount to an arbitrary address, whether an EOA or smart contract, and have full control over funds originally intended for the protocol and users.  

This could cause irreparable damage to the reputation of the protocol, as well as loss of funds to the users.

