# Vulnerability details

 ## Impact

The `execute()` function contains a critical reentrancy vulnerability. The function uses the `call()` function to send ETH to the specified address along with provided data. This can potentially lead to a reentrancy attack if the provided address is a smart contract with a malicious fallback function.

## Proof of Concept

In the `execute()` function. The `call()` function does not block the execution of the calling contract, so the calling contract could be reentered by the malicious fallback function of the contract that is called.

The `call` function is used to send ETH to the address `_to` along with the `_data`. This could potentially lead to a vulnerability if `_to` is a smart contract with a fallback function that can perform malicious actions upon receiving ETH.

**[execute function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-dopex/blob/0ea4387a4851cd6c8811dfb61da95a677f3f63ae/contracts/amo/UniV3LiquidityAmo.sol#L339-L346)**
