# Vulnerability details

`PerpetualAtlanticVault._updateFundingRate()` is called during `purchase()` and `payFunding()`, to distribute the premium/funding to `PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP` evenly throughput the epoch in a drip manner. 

However, it does not properly handle the case where `endTime == startTime`, where the current time is equal to the end of the epoch. That means when `purchase()` and `payFunding()` are called exactly at the epoch end time, the premium/funding are not distributed to the `PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP` and will be stuck in `PerpetualAtlanticVault`.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-dopex/blob/main/contracts/perp-vault/PerpetualAtlanticVault.sol#L594-L614
```Solidity
  function _updateFundingRate(uint256 amount) private {
    if (fundingRates[latestFundingPaymentPointer] == 0) {
      uint256 startTime;
      if (lastUpdateTime > nextFundingPaymentTimestamp() - fundingDuration) {
        startTime = lastUpdateTime;
      } else {
        startTime = nextFundingPaymentTimestamp() - fundingDuration;
      }
      uint256 endTime = nextFundingPaymentTimestamp();

      fundingRates[latestFundingPaymentPointer] =
        (amount * 1e18) /
        (endTime - startTime);
    } else {
      uint256 startTime = lastUpdateTime;
      uint256 endTime = nextFundingPaymentTimestamp();

      //@audit when endTime == startTime, amount should be directly transferred to PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP
      if (endTime == startTime) return;
      fundingRates[latestFundingPaymentPointer] =
        fundingRates[latestFundingPaymentPointer] +
        ((amount * 1e18) / (endTime - startTime));
    }
  }
```

## Impact
 `PerpetualAtlanticVaultLP` holders will lose the premium/funding when the issue occur.


