# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The emergencyWithdraw function in the provided Solidity contract has potential vulnerabilities that could lead to a Denial of Service (DoS) based on an unbounded loop & external call. These vulnerabilities could prevent the function from executing successfully, which could in turn prevent the admin from withdrawing tokens in an emergency. This could have serious implications for the liquidity and operation of the contract.

This is High Risk because, due to the nature of the function, the developers wants instant withdrawal, any delay could lead to even severe loss of funds.

## Proof of Concept
